  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Eastern Hoolock Gibbon in Eastern Assam- Arunachal Pradesh landscape through education-awareness &amp; community conservation practices (CHGAAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to create a strong cadre of trained teachers who can educate and motivate students and together with students motivate the community for positive actions, find sacred groves for gibbon conservation taking into consideration taboos and beliefs of local communities, promote local youth involvement in Eastern Hoolock Gibbon (EHG) conservation in their villages, construct canopy bridges in the selected fragments of Lower Dibang valley district for gibbon use, and identify potential eco-tourism spots with gibbon as target species involving the youth volunteers and local community.</narrative>
  </description>
